      "releaseNotes": "What's new\n\n• Meet the redesigned Copilot experience in GitHub Mobile - chat, code, and keep work moving wherever you are.\n  • Find chat and coding sessions together in the unified Copilot tab, and go from asking questions to making code changes in the same conversation.\n  • Start cloud sessions quickly in secure, isolated sandboxes that save your progress so you can resume later without relying on your computer.\n  • Describe tasks using voice input or attach images and files to give Copilot more context.\n  • Start a cloud session on your phone and continue on the web or desktop, with sessions and pinned items synced across web and mobile.\n  • Use slash commands directly in your conversations.\n  • The new experience is available on paid Copilot plans, subject to your organization’s policies. Copilot Free users can continue using Copilot Chat.\n• Official Support for iPhone Duo including updated UI layouts.\n\nBug fixes\n\n• Remote PDFs no longer crash when Apple Intelligence reads them.\n• The settings icon on your profile matches the other icons.\n• Fixed the emoji picker closing right after it opens when you set your status.\n• Pull request lists in a repository let you reset filters when nothing matches.\n• The emoji picker when setting your status doesn't get cut off.",
      "version": "1.283.0",
